From b33035aba4fe0c684ee8b53c0c7d744b118d2e3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:40:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] fix(config): refuse unknown tool names in
 enabled_tools, opt_in_tools and disabled_tools

Toolset names are validated at start (a typo in `toolsets` exits with
"invalid toolset name"), but tool names were not. A misspelt entry was
accepted silently:

- `enabled_tools = ["resources_gett"]` started a server that served no
  tools at all;
- `disabled_tools = ["pods_deleet"]` started a server that still served
  pods_delete, the tool the operator meant to hide;
- `opt_in_tools` (#1597) has the same shape.

The server now checks the three lists when it is created and when a new
configuration is loaded: every name must be a tool that one of the
server's toolsets provides (after the target-list rename). A tool of a
toolset that is not enabled is a valid name; it is simply not served, as
documented for opt_in_tools. Otherwise the server refuses to start, or
rejects the reload, with an error that names the unknown entries.

The check does not run when tools are re-applied after a cluster-state
change, so a tool that a toolset offers only when the cluster has some
API cannot stop a running server. Toolsets are asked for their tools
with the server's cluster inspector, as when tools are applied.
docs/configuration.md says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
