 | Field | Type | Default | Description |
 |-------|------|---------|-------------|
-| `enabled_tools` | string[] | `[]` | Allowlist of specific tools to enable. When set, only these tools are registered. See [Cluster authorization](#cluster-authorization). |
-| `opt_in_tools` | string[] | `[]` | Additional tools to enable on top of the current selection, whether that is the default selection or an explicit `enabled_tools` allowlist. |
-| `disabled_tools` | string[] | `[]` | Denylist of specific tools to unregister. Applied after `enabled_tools`. See [Cluster authorization](#cluster-authorization). |
+| `enabled_tools` | string[] | `[]` | Allowlist of specific tools to enable. When set, only these tools are registered. Every name must be a tool of a toolset this server provides, or the server refuses to start (or to reload). See [Cluster authorization](#cluster-authorization). |
+| `opt_in_tools` | string[] | `[]` | Additional tools to enable on top of the current selection, whether that is the default selection or an explicit `enabled_tools` allowlist. Every name must be a tool of a toolset this server provides, or the server refuses to start (or to reload). |
+| `disabled_tools` | string[] | `[]` | Denylist of specific tools to unregister. Applied after `enabled_tools`. Every name must be a tool of a toolset this server provides, or the server refuses to start (or to reload). See [Cluster authorization](#cluster-authorization). |
 
 The owning toolset must be enabled in `toolsets` for a tool to be available. Neither `enabled_tools` nor `opt_in_tools` enables a toolset automatically. All selections remain subject to `read_only`, `disable_destructive`, and other tool availability filters.
 
